WEBVTT

1
00:00:14.670 --> 00:00:19.372
Long, long ago two boys were born on the same day in the same city.

2
00:00:20.392 --> 00:00:25.294
Tom Canty was born to a poor family, who couldn't afford another child.

3
00:00:26.815 --> 00:00:32.535
Prince Edward was born to a royal family, who welcomed the new heir to the throne.

4
00:00:35.858 --> 00:00:39.281
A dozen years later, both boys lived by the river.

5
00:00:41.243 --> 00:00:47.528
While Edward lived in a magnificent palace, Tom lived in a shabby room in a poor neighborhood.

6
00:00:50.311 --> 00:00:55.616
While Edward's father was King Henry, Tom's father was John Canty, a thief.

7
00:00:58.036 --> 00:01:01.898
John often made Tom and his sister, Nancy, beg for money.

8
00:01:07.840 --> 00:01:12.682
As Tom headed out to beg one January morning, he met Father Andrew.

9
00:01:14.623 --> 00:01:18.745
The priest had taught him how to read and write as well as some Latin.

10
00:01:19.946 --> 00:01:25.148
But what Tom liked best were Father Andrew's tales of palaces and princes.

11
00:01:27.896 --> 00:01:30.137
"Do you have a story for me today, Father?"

12
00:01:30.457 --> 00:01:31.317
Tom asked.

13
00:01:31.337 --> 00:01:32.778
"Of course!"

14
00:01:33.278 --> 00:01:35.279
the priest said as they walked together.

15
00:01:35.299 --> 00:01:44.803
"Once upon a time there was a prince named Richard Because of Father Andrew's wonderful stories, Tom sometimes

16
00:01:44.883 --> 00:01:46.324
pretended to be a prince.

17
00:01:47.664 --> 00:01:53.426
This amused his friends, but they also enjoyed his game—except when he made them the servants.

18
00:01:56.048 --> 00:02:00.462
All too soon Tom and Father Andrew arrived at the priest's church.

19
00:02:00.482 --> 00:02:06.086
"We'll finish Prince Richard's story later," Father Andrew said.

20
00:02:06.106 --> 00:02:08.448
"I can't wait!"

21
00:02:10.929 --> 00:02:12.030
Then Tom sighed.

22
00:02:12.050 --> 00:02:15.512
"It's time to ask strangers for money."

23
00:02:20.476 --> 00:02:23.698
Tom hated begging, but his family needed the money.

24
00:02:25.299 --> 00:02:31.110
Most people ignored him, so he was surprised when someone tapped his shoulder later that day.

25
00:02:31.130 --> 00:02:33.071
"What's this?

26
00:02:33.491 --> 00:02:34.791
A prince begging?"

27
00:02:38.193 --> 00:02:42.234
Tom turned to find his best friend, Julian Witt, laughing.

28
00:02:42.254 --> 00:02:47.176
"You have mocked royalty and are sentenced to prison!"

29
00:02:47.696 --> 00:02:48.417
Tom joked.

30
00:02:49.537 --> 00:02:53.019
Then, in his regular voice, he added, "I need a break.

31
00:02:53.839 --> 00:02:56.020
Let's see if anybody wants to play by the river."

32
00:02:58.004 --> 00:02:59.384
Julian turned pale.

33
00:02:59.404 --> 00:03:00.605
"The river?"

34
00:03:00.625 --> 00:03:04.006
"Oh, sorry!

35
00:03:04.026 --> 00:03:06.266
I forgot about what happened to you there.

36
00:03:07.227 --> 00:03:09.027
We'll stay away from the water today."

37
00:03:11.328 --> 00:03:14.669
The boys found their friends, and the afternoon passed quickly.

38
00:03:16.689 --> 00:03:22.531
Prince Tom pardoned Julian, gave orders to his army, and met with his royal advisers.

39
00:03:22.551 --> 00:03:27.985
"Your Highness, the sun is setting," Julian said.

40
00:03:28.005 --> 00:03:30.766
"Oh no!"

41
00:03:31.326 --> 00:03:32.147
Tom gulped.

42
00:03:32.967 --> 00:03:35.228
"I have only one coin for my father!"

43
00:03:37.990 --> 00:03:42.732
For a moment Tom thought about not going home, but he didn't want to miss supper.

44
00:03:45.454 --> 00:03:48.656
Reluctantly, he said good-bye and headed home.

45
00:03:54.138 --> 00:03:55.039
have you been?"

46
00:03:55.419 --> 00:03:56.600
Tom's father yelled.

47
00:03:57.696 --> 00:03:59.478
"You'd better have lots of money!"

48
00:03:59.498 --> 00:04:02.860
"People weren't in a generous mood."

49
00:04:04.702 --> 00:04:06.543
Tom handed over his one coin.

50
00:04:06.563 --> 00:04:10.466
"'A generous mood.'"

51
00:04:10.947 --> 00:04:13.048
John Canty echoed Tom's words.

52
00:04:13.068 --> 00:04:15.831
"Where do you learn this stuff?

53
00:04:17.072 --> 00:04:18.773
Probably from that priest."

54
00:04:20.074 --> 00:04:21.755
That reminded Tom of something.

55
00:04:21.775 --> 00:04:27.060
"I wonder if Father Andrew has any books about Prince Richard," he thought.

56
00:04:28.276 --> 00:04:31.017
"Maybe I could—" "Are you listening?"

57
00:04:31.457 --> 00:04:32.297
John shouted.

58
00:04:32.317 --> 00:04:34.878
"I said, go to bed!"

59
00:04:34.898 --> 00:04:41.960
"Oh, don't send him to bed without supper," Tom's mother pleaded.

60
00:04:43.061 --> 00:04:46.062
Meanwhile Nancy tried to stay out of her father's way.

61
00:04:46.082 --> 00:04:49.043
"Don't interfere!"

62
00:04:49.443 --> 00:04:50.583
John said to his wife.

63
00:04:50.603 --> 00:04:52.784
"To bed, Tom!

64
00:04:53.104 --> 00:04:58.963
Now!" Tom went to a corner and untangled some old blankets.

65
00:05:00.724 --> 00:05:05.248
He made himself as comfortable as possible on the straw covering the wood floor.

66
00:05:06.669 --> 00:05:11.353
But for a long time, his hunger and his parents' arguing kept him awake.

67
00:05:13.655 --> 00:05:15.456
He tried to distract himself.

68
00:05:15.476 --> 00:05:21.161
"How many princes has Father Andrew told me about?"

69
00:05:21.722 --> 00:05:22.402
Tom thought.

70
00:05:25.052 --> 00:05:32.115
"William, Richard, James Tom drifted off, thinking of a distant kingdom.

71
00:05:33.336 --> 00:05:39.718
In his dream he was surrounded by lords and ladies, beautiful music, and delicious food.

72
00:05:41.539 --> 00:05:45.221
Everyone bowed to Prince Tom and obeyed his orders.

73
00:05:48.862 --> 00:05:53.244
The next morning Tom awoke in the same filthy room on Offal Street.

74
00:05:55.620 --> 00:05:59.061
He was still hungry and still wearing his ragged clothes.

75
00:06:02.942 --> 00:06:04.623
Tom sighed with disappointment.

76
00:06:04.643 --> 00:06:12.005
"I'll only be a prince in my dreams," he thought, slipping outside before anyone else woke up.

77
00:06:12.025 --> 00:06:15.246
"But maybe someday I'll meet a real one."

78
00:06:19.207 --> 00:06:23.868
As Tom wandered along the river, he lost track of time and where he was.

79
00:06:25.232 --> 00:06:28.653
After a while he came upon a magnificent building.

80
00:06:30.413 --> 00:06:31.994
Tom's eyes grew wide.

81
00:06:32.014 --> 00:06:34.835
"Could this be the king's palace?"

82
00:06:36.255 --> 00:06:38.976
He joined a few people waiting near a golden gate.

83
00:06:40.816 --> 00:06:44.957
Suddenly a boy and a man appeared in the courtyard beyond the gate.

84
00:06:46.738 --> 00:06:50.479
Dressed in silk and velvet, the boy wore a sword at his hip.

85
00:06:52.399 --> 00:06:55.005
Tom heard the man call the boy "Your Highness."

86
00:06:55.025 --> 00:06:56.986
"A prince!"

87
00:06:58.227 --> 00:07:00.188
Tom rushed forward for a better look.

88
00:07:01.089 --> 00:07:05.092
Immediately a guard grabbed Tom's hand and jerked him away.

89
00:07:07.133 --> 00:07:08.554
"Step back, you pauper!"

90
00:07:12.797 --> 00:07:14.098
The people laughed.

91
00:07:15.739 --> 00:07:18.862
But the prince ran to the gate and scolded the guard.

92
00:07:18.882 --> 00:07:21.984
"How dare you treat a poor boy like that!

93
00:07:23.081 --> 00:07:25.390
Open the gate at once, and let him in!"
